;; The module _signal (PY6f; Modules/signalmodule.c): the process's signals delivered to Python handlers.
;; signal(n, callable) has os/signal notify one channel; its receiver goroutine marks the signal pending (the C
;; handler's trip_signal), sets the eval breaker, wakes the main thread when it blocks and writes the wakeup fd;
;; the main thread runs the handlers at its next check (thread_gil.go). SIG_IGN is signal.Ignore, SIG_DFL
;; signal.Reset. raise_signal and os.kill of the own process run the handler before they return, as on Linux.
;; The interval timers (alarm, setitimer) are Go timers sending the signal; pthread_sigmask's mask is kept here:
;; a blocked signal stays pending (sigpending, sigwait) until unblocked.

